1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,956
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:06,956 --> 00:00:10,891
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,891 --> 00:00:13,062
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,062 --> 00:00:15,729
When you hug other people,
the world doesn’t have to stop spinning.

5
00:00:15,729 --> 00:00:16,941
What if I lose?

6
00:00:16,941 --> 00:00:18,077
Will I still get my reward?

7
00:00:18,077 --> 00:00:20,150
This isn’t a prize for the winner.

8
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:21,990
It’s a reward for being amazing.

9
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:23,900
Try giving the people around you a chance.

10
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,480
Let them be a part of your life too.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,045
I’m quitting.

12
00:00:27,045 --> 00:00:27,973
I don’t want to do judo anymore.

13
00:00:27,973 --> 00:00:29,836
Why do you think I need someone?

14
00:00:29,836 --> 00:00:32,593
If you know you’re amazing,
come and hug Cheewa.

15
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,654
Just like that, the sky's full of stars, huh?

16
00:01:37,733 --> 00:01:38,392
Isn’t it pretty?

17
00:01:39,614 --> 00:01:40,337
Yeah, it’s pretty.

18
00:01:43,748 --> 00:01:47,608
Hugging me made you feel better, right?

19
00:01:50,435 --> 00:01:51,453
What? Who hugged you?

20
00:01:52,675 --> 00:01:53,790
You were the one who hugged me.

21
00:01:55,523 --> 00:01:58,171
But you were the one
who stepped toward me.

22
00:02:01,153 --> 00:02:01,799
Nonsense.

23
00:02:05,776 --> 00:02:08,210
If we refer to the free hug at the canteen,

24
00:02:08,757 --> 00:02:10,860
when you opened your arms to me,

25
00:02:12,410 --> 00:02:15,602
I took two steps toward you.

26
00:02:15,967 --> 00:02:19,669
Earlier, I was the one
who opened my arms to you

27
00:02:19,669 --> 00:02:22,003
and you walked two steps toward me.

28
00:02:22,167 --> 00:02:23,553
That means

29
00:02:23,553 --> 00:02:26,105
you were the one
who walked over to hug me.

30
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,057
If you know you’re amazing,

31
00:02:29,768 --> 00:02:31,514
come and hug Cheewa.

32
00:02:51,349 --> 00:02:52,842
I’m right here.

33
00:02:59,508 --> 00:03:00,108
Nah.

34
00:03:04,066 --> 00:03:05,401
Go home and sleep, nerd.

35
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,859
I still want to look at the stars.

36
00:03:09,133 --> 00:03:11,260
Then go do that in your room.

37
00:03:12,373 --> 00:03:14,319
Did you know I’m free this Saturday?

38
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:16,430
And?

39
00:03:17,634 --> 00:03:19,427
Do you want to go to the planetarium
with me?

40
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:27,371
Why should I go with you?

41
00:03:30,198 --> 00:03:31,750
It’s really beautiful there.

42
00:03:32,242 --> 00:03:33,892
If you don’t go, you’ll regret it.

43
00:03:34,567 --> 00:03:35,752
Who's going to regret it,

44
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,946
P’Niran or Nong Parncheewa?

45
00:03:38,366 --> 00:03:42,296
If P’Niran doesn’t go,
will Nong Parncheewa cry like a baby?

46
00:03:43,646 --> 00:03:44,679
I won’t cry.

47
00:03:45,153 --> 00:03:46,862
I’m just asking.

48
00:03:46,862 --> 00:03:48,255
If you don’t want to go, it’s fine.

49
00:03:51,119 --> 00:03:53,280
It’s just that watching the stars alone

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,460
is a little lonely.

51
00:04:03,582 --> 00:04:04,296
Alright.

52
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:05,978
We can go.

53
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:09,121
I’d be bored at home anyway.

54
00:04:11,693 --> 00:04:12,855
Did you know—

55
00:04:13,037 --> 00:04:13,792
I’m not going anymore.

56
00:04:22,194 --> 00:04:23,548
Hey, I’m just kidding.

57
00:04:30,692 --> 00:04:31,672
P’Niran,

58
00:04:32,712 --> 00:04:34,178
if you’re still sad,

59
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:37,125
we can keep watching the stars.

60
00:04:39,909 --> 00:04:41,074
I’m not in a rush tonight.

61
00:04:43,917 --> 00:04:44,495
Mm.

62
00:04:54,035 --> 00:04:56,386
Or we can go stargazing in my room
if you want.

63
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:00,989
You’re wicked.

64
00:05:09,224 --> 00:05:10,600
Ugh, it’s Saturday.

65
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:14,061
Why do I have to wake up so early?

66
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:42,836
Dad’s out of town for three days.

67
00:05:43,201 --> 00:05:44,657
Go eat at Auntie Tang’s.

68
00:05:44,912 --> 00:05:46,081
Give it your all at practice.

69
00:05:53,414 --> 00:05:54,124
Have you been waiting long?

70
00:05:54,489 --> 00:05:55,267
Not long.

71
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:57,979
What are you taking me to do today?

72
00:05:58,946 --> 00:06:00,011
You’ll find out soon.

73
00:06:00,503 --> 00:06:01,840
I can't get you to spill, huh?

74
00:06:02,533 --> 00:06:03,238
No.

75
00:06:03,311 --> 00:06:04,713
Where are you going?

76
00:06:04,713 --> 00:06:06,056
Are you going on a date?

77
00:06:10,753 --> 00:06:11,511
Do you know him?

78
00:06:11,821 --> 00:06:12,535
Yeah.

79
00:06:12,535 --> 00:06:15,513
Kaomao, did you run away from your mom
to get out of homework today?

80
00:06:16,990 --> 00:06:17,559
Let’s go.

81
00:06:20,787 --> 00:06:21,545
Come on.

82
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:23,529
Is that yummy?

83
00:06:38,446 --> 00:06:39,999
Do you want to switch seats with me?

84
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:42,252
It’s fine. I’ll sit here.

85
00:06:51,610 --> 00:06:52,392
Use my hat.

86
00:06:54,399 --> 00:06:55,056
Thank you.

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,086
Want a fan?

88
00:07:02,636 --> 00:07:03,489
Thank you.

89
00:07:10,548 --> 00:07:12,061
You like listening to tapes and old music?

90
00:07:14,888 --> 00:07:15,585
Yes.

91
00:07:16,679 --> 00:07:17,783
Just like my dad.

92
00:07:17,984 --> 00:07:19,372
We have a record player at home.

93
00:07:19,372 --> 00:07:20,375
He loves playing records.

94
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:39,535
Can I come over
and listen with you sometime?

95
00:07:41,487 --> 00:07:42,274
Yeah.

96
00:07:49,843 --> 00:07:51,246
It’s closed for renovation.

97
00:07:51,903 --> 00:07:52,666
Yeah.

98
00:07:55,164 --> 00:07:56,898
I’m sorry I didn't check beforehand.

99
00:07:57,354 --> 00:07:58,550
Now we can’t go stargazing.

100
00:08:00,137 --> 00:08:01,387
It’s fine.

101
00:08:02,135 --> 00:08:03,689
Let’s find something fun to do instead.

102
00:08:05,112 --> 00:08:07,134
Or do you have any ideas?

103
00:08:07,425 --> 00:08:08,988
It doesn’t have to be academic.

104
00:08:09,872 --> 00:08:11,152
Let’s go somewhere else.

105
00:08:16,059 --> 00:08:17,903
I bet it’s still going to be academic.

106
00:08:19,289 --> 00:08:21,100
Did you not hear a word I said?

107
00:08:21,592 --> 00:08:23,477
This is not that educational.

108
00:08:23,896 --> 00:08:25,818
Consider it an eye-opening experience.

109
00:08:26,274 --> 00:08:27,025
You might like it.

110
00:08:27,755 --> 00:08:28,819
No way.

111
00:08:33,981 --> 00:08:35,166
Should we go somewhere else?

112
00:08:36,388 --> 00:08:37,801
We came all this way,
so we have to do some sightseeing.

113
00:08:38,968 --> 00:08:39,585
Sightseeing?

114
00:08:39,822 --> 00:08:41,321
You call this sightseeing?

115
00:08:41,777 --> 00:08:43,274
Come on, Glasses.

116
00:08:43,985 --> 00:08:45,985
I feel like I’m on a field trip.

117
00:08:48,010 --> 00:08:49,823
If you really don’t like this,

118
00:08:52,231 --> 00:08:53,678
we can go home.

119
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,493
Oh, your face fell.

120
00:08:57,493 --> 00:08:58,722
Why do you look so sad?

121
00:08:58,722 --> 00:08:59,505
Come on.

122
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,602
Fine. We can hang out here.

123
00:09:03,627 --> 00:09:04,839
Let’s go to the next room.

124
00:09:07,593 --> 00:09:08,397
You’re smiling like a kid.

125
00:09:10,203 --> 00:09:12,784
Can I be your little kid, P’Niran?

126
00:09:19,771 --> 00:09:20,460
Are you hungry?

127
00:09:21,627 --> 00:09:23,461
Yeah, a little bit.

128
00:09:23,461 --> 00:09:24,682
I didn’t have breakfast.

129
00:09:26,469 --> 00:09:28,475
Then we can grab something to eat first.

130
00:09:31,685 --> 00:09:32,459
That sounds good.

131
00:09:33,553 --> 00:09:35,108
A little something to make up for
not getting to see the stars today.

132
00:09:36,841 --> 00:09:37,877
What do you mean?

133
00:09:38,971 --> 00:09:39,734
The fried egg.

134
00:09:41,339 --> 00:09:42,190
That’s your star.

135
00:09:43,777 --> 00:09:44,979
You can look at it on your plate for now.

136
00:09:46,092 --> 00:09:47,657
So creative.

137
00:09:57,890 --> 00:10:00,308
Oh, what’s with that face?

138
00:10:00,454 --> 00:10:01,115
Is it not good?

139
00:10:01,717 --> 00:10:02,807
It’s too spicy.

140
00:10:03,099 --> 00:10:04,171
Okay, then just eat the egg.

141
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:05,416
Do you want to order something else?

142
00:10:05,416 --> 00:10:06,169
I’ll eat that for you.

143
00:10:07,136 --> 00:10:08,023
I can eat it.

144
00:10:13,968 --> 00:10:15,449
Here, eat your star.

145
00:10:16,397 --> 00:10:18,203
If you can’t eat the rest, it’s fine.

146
00:10:18,404 --> 00:10:19,401
Thank you.

147
00:10:19,401 --> 00:10:20,105
But…

148
00:10:20,105 --> 00:10:21,131
Stop talking. Just eat.

149
00:10:26,019 --> 00:10:27,559
What are you taking me to see?

150
00:10:27,687 --> 00:10:29,131
It’s an illusion.

151
00:10:29,131 --> 00:10:31,183
It’s an optical illusion that tricks your brain.

152
00:10:31,183 --> 00:10:32,599
You really like this kind of stuff, huh?

153
00:10:32,781 --> 00:10:34,133
Or do you want to skip a step
and be friends?

154
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:35,770
You can.

155
00:10:46,149 --> 00:10:49,648
Who knew coffee and the universe
could be the same color?

156
00:10:50,004 --> 00:10:52,193
Now you and I know.

157
00:10:52,415 --> 00:10:54,671
From now on, whenever you drink a latte,

158
00:10:54,671 --> 00:10:57,980
you’ll think of the color Cosmic Latte
and think of me.

159
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,126
You really like this kind of stuff, huh?

160
00:11:24,638 --> 00:11:25,280
Yes.

161
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,843
It’s interesting.

162
00:11:27,888 --> 00:11:31,707
There’s so much more in this world
humans haven’t discovered yet.

163
00:11:32,330 --> 00:11:33,714
I want to find it.

164
00:11:34,203 --> 00:11:36,036
I’m fascinated by these things.

165
00:11:38,171 --> 00:11:40,154
(When people like something,)

166
00:11:40,443 --> 00:11:41,978
(you can see it in their eyes, right?)

167
00:11:42,423 --> 00:11:44,040
(Like Cheewa right now.)

168
00:11:44,485 --> 00:11:45,941
(He looks so happy.)

169
00:11:47,097 --> 00:11:49,834
(It’s nice to like something)

170
00:11:50,056 --> 00:11:51,389
(and be able to enjoy it.)

171
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:54,533
And what about you?

172
00:11:56,601 --> 00:11:57,265
Huh?

173
00:11:58,421 --> 00:11:59,798
Me? Oh.

174
00:12:00,154 --> 00:12:01,427
You mean what I’m fascinated by?

175
00:12:01,716 --> 00:12:02,396
Yes.

176
00:12:03,396 --> 00:12:04,690
Hmm…

177
00:12:07,625 --> 00:12:08,448
It’s hard to say.

178
00:12:09,182 --> 00:12:11,152
I’m feeling kind of lost right now.

179
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:13,921
What I thought I really liked,

180
00:12:15,366 --> 00:12:17,716
I don’t think I like it that much anymore.

181
00:12:19,806 --> 00:12:22,317
But when I think about quitting, I feel empty.

182
00:12:22,317 --> 00:12:23,438
I can’t really explain it.

183
00:12:24,839 --> 00:12:26,426
I just can’t seem to let it go.

184
00:12:28,116 --> 00:12:29,358
It’s frustrating, isn’t it?

185
00:12:29,736 --> 00:12:30,884
I feel like I’m so indecisive.

186
00:12:32,374 --> 00:12:33,563
Hey, don’t stress.

187
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:36,969
I… am fine.

188
00:12:38,236 --> 00:12:40,504
I can watch you enjoy what you like.

189
00:12:40,504 --> 00:12:41,163
I’m totally fine.

190
00:12:41,875 --> 00:12:42,650
I mean it.

191
00:12:44,295 --> 00:12:45,469
Let’s check out the next one.

192
00:12:46,759 --> 00:12:47,451
Come on.

193
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,934
What’s this one?

194
00:12:53,668 --> 00:12:54,537
No.

195
00:12:55,449 --> 00:12:56,828
I see it differently.

196
00:13:00,141 --> 00:13:00,779
How?

197
00:13:03,114 --> 00:13:04,791
Let me give you an easy explanation.

198
00:13:05,836 --> 00:13:08,035
It’s like the theory of gravity.

199
00:13:09,013 --> 00:13:10,107
Gravity again?

200
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:15,459
Gravity is the attractive force
that Earth exerts on all objects

201
00:13:15,793 --> 00:13:17,373
Just like my interests.

202
00:13:19,352 --> 00:13:21,155
When I’m interested in something,

203
00:13:21,399 --> 00:13:25,002
I try to draw it toward me,
creating a gravitational pull.

204
00:13:26,558 --> 00:13:28,541
But when I feel like it isn’t right for me

205
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:30,951
and I don’t enjoy doing it
or feel happy doing it,

206
00:13:31,751 --> 00:13:33,827
I’ll slowly stop attracting it.

207
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:37,521
I’ll enter a state of zero gravity.

208
00:13:39,278 --> 00:13:40,711
In the end,

209
00:13:41,334 --> 00:13:45,721
time will make us
drift out of each other’s orbit.

210
00:13:46,032 --> 00:13:46,908
Do you get it?

211
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:48,671
Ah.

212
00:13:51,006 --> 00:13:54,033
Is that a science kid’s idea
of a simple explanation?

213
00:13:54,278 --> 00:13:55,368
Sorry.

214
00:13:56,035 --> 00:13:57,363
You might not understand.

215
00:13:58,097 --> 00:14:01,267
Thank you, though.

216
00:14:06,181 --> 00:14:09,104
There’s inert gas and plasma
circulating inside.

217
00:14:10,968 --> 00:14:13,407
If we touch it, it’ll keep following us.

218
00:14:13,674 --> 00:14:14,909
Do you want to try?

219
00:14:16,065 --> 00:14:16,789
I’m good.

220
00:14:18,012 --> 00:14:19,410
You can touch it. It won’t shock you.

221
00:14:19,410 --> 00:14:21,148
You do it. I’m good. I’m grown up.

222
00:14:22,638 --> 00:14:23,420
Hey.

223
00:14:24,421 --> 00:14:25,267
No.

224
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:33,981
I’m just like inert gas and plasma.

225
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:37,700
.What are you talking about?

226
00:14:40,835 --> 00:14:42,783
I keep following you.

227
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:46,224
You’re such a kid.

228
00:14:46,746 --> 00:14:48,963
I have to touch you first,
and then you’ll follow me, right?

229
00:14:52,968 --> 00:14:55,292
We're only a few years apart.

230
00:14:56,804 --> 00:14:57,473
And?

231
00:14:57,895 --> 00:15:01,129
I’m not that much more of a kid than you.

232
00:15:01,129 --> 00:15:02,903
You want a judo athlete to throw you?

233
00:15:04,215 --> 00:15:04,917
No.

234
00:15:05,146 --> 00:15:07,525
What? It’s obvious.

235
00:15:08,058 --> 00:15:09,166
Cheewa, Grade 11.

236
00:15:09,344 --> 00:15:10,390
Niran, Grade 12.

237
00:15:11,769 --> 00:15:13,082
Isn’t that right?

238
00:15:13,594 --> 00:15:15,579
We’re a senior and a little kid.

239
00:15:16,735 --> 00:15:18,248
Or do you want to skip a step
and be friends?

240
00:15:20,499 --> 00:15:21,240
Hmm…

241
00:15:22,968 --> 00:15:25,679
But honestly, I don’t care much about age.

242
00:15:26,324 --> 00:15:27,454
We can be friends if you want.

243
00:15:36,048 --> 00:15:37,432
These look like jellyfish.

244
00:15:45,308 --> 00:15:46,894
Even after having coffee,

245
00:15:47,561 --> 00:15:48,669
I’m still so sleepy.

246
00:15:48,669 --> 00:15:52,162
Did you know coffee doesn't actually
stop you from feeling sleepy?

247
00:15:52,273 --> 00:15:54,016
It just tricks your brain.

248
00:15:54,438 --> 00:15:56,053
Yeah, yeah, I believe you.

249
00:15:56,764 --> 00:15:58,056
Save your explanation for later.

250
00:16:07,131 --> 00:16:09,231
Is this smell from fabric softener or perfume?

251
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:13,888
I put on a little perfume.

252
00:16:13,888 --> 00:16:14,845
Well, look at you,

253
00:16:15,312 --> 00:16:17,109
wearing perfume when you're still so young.

254
00:16:17,287 --> 00:16:18,710
You stole your dad's, didn't you?

255
00:16:20,467 --> 00:16:21,223
Yes.

256
00:16:22,224 --> 00:16:22,956
Why?

257
00:16:23,712 --> 00:16:25,094
You don’t like it?

258
00:16:25,968 --> 00:16:27,687
It smells nice.

259
00:16:35,208 --> 00:16:36,848
Are we going to be here for a while?

260
00:16:37,137 --> 00:16:39,104
If so, can I take a nap?

261
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:43,396
You can. I’ll be quiet.

262
00:17:00,285 --> 00:17:01,356
Can I listen too?

263
00:17:23,223 --> 00:17:24,800
The cord's too tight.

264
00:18:00,728 --> 00:18:01,460
Oh.

265
00:18:02,016 --> 00:18:03,183
I got this for you.

266
00:18:03,183 --> 00:18:04,326
I know you love reading,

267
00:18:04,326 --> 00:18:05,459
so I figured it would suit you.

268
00:18:09,684 --> 00:18:10,875
Thank you.

269
00:18:11,297 --> 00:18:12,812
This is cute.

270
00:18:14,591 --> 00:18:15,209
Just like me.

271
00:18:16,476 --> 00:18:18,063
Do you feel better after your nap?

272
00:18:19,108 --> 00:18:21,785
Yeah, but I wanted to sleep a little longer.

273
00:18:22,252 --> 00:18:23,458
Someone woke me up.

274
00:18:24,547 --> 00:18:25,488
You did.

275
00:18:29,423 --> 00:18:32,122
Should we come back here together sometime?

276
00:18:34,079 --> 00:18:35,368
Huh? What did you say?

277
00:18:35,368 --> 00:18:36,192
I couldn’t hear you properly.

278
00:18:39,327 --> 00:18:41,991
Were there stars in your dream earlier?

279
00:18:42,436 --> 00:18:45,697
And did you like the songs I played?

280
00:18:48,142 --> 00:18:49,582
I don’t think that’s what you said.

281
00:18:52,528 --> 00:18:53,483
Fine.

282
00:18:53,483 --> 00:18:54,702
I won’t push you.

283
00:18:57,348 --> 00:19:00,371
If I say I don’t remember, will you get pouty?

284
00:19:00,371 --> 00:19:01,655
Both the songs and the dream.

285
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,362
No, I won’t.

286
00:19:04,362 --> 00:19:05,621
Okay, I don’t remember.

287
00:19:06,710 --> 00:19:08,892
You can play the songs for me later.

288
00:19:10,026 --> 00:19:10,732
Okay.

289
00:19:15,579 --> 00:19:17,430
It's actually pretty nice being here.

290
00:19:18,253 --> 00:19:23,602
I get to look back on things
when I talk to you.

291
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,050
Even though I can’t find a solution,

292
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,594
it helps clear my head

293
00:19:31,372 --> 00:19:32,774
just venting to someone.

294
00:19:37,977 --> 00:19:39,392
Did you know

295
00:19:39,815 --> 00:19:45,310
the Astronomy Club stargazes on the science building rooftop during breaks?

296
00:19:46,968 --> 00:19:49,278
There’s a meteor shower
around that time too.

297
00:19:50,434 --> 00:19:53,316
If the sky is clear, we’ll probably see it.

298
00:19:54,606 --> 00:19:56,050
Come join if you’re interested.

299
00:19:57,339 --> 00:20:01,066
To make up for
missing the planetarium today.

300
00:20:03,801 --> 00:20:04,835
That’s interesting.

301
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:09,779
I don’t think I have to be
at the athletes’ village that month.

302
00:20:10,379 --> 00:20:12,199
I’ll probably be so damn free.

303
00:20:13,528 --> 00:20:14,514
That’s actually nice.

304
00:20:16,293 --> 00:20:18,339
I can just lie down
and look at the real stars instead.

305
00:20:18,339 --> 00:20:21,091
But it probably won’t be as clear as
seeing them in the planetarium.

306
00:20:21,847 --> 00:20:23,124
That’s fine.

307
00:20:24,725 --> 00:20:26,909
Do you want to keep walking around?

308
00:20:27,048 --> 00:20:27,855
Sure.

309
00:20:28,077 --> 00:20:29,267
I don’t want to go home yet anyway.

310
00:20:30,223 --> 00:20:33,409
Or do you want to go somewhere else?

311
00:20:33,698 --> 00:20:35,193
I can take you anywhere.

312
00:20:38,350 --> 00:20:39,752
Well,

313
00:20:40,552 --> 00:20:41,994
if I want to go to Mars,

314
00:20:42,150 --> 00:20:43,152
can you take me there?

315
00:20:48,711 --> 00:20:49,703
I’m just kidding.

316
00:20:52,549 --> 00:20:54,046
Just wait until I grow up.

317
00:20:54,735 --> 00:20:56,638
I’ll build a spaceship.

318
00:20:57,150 --> 00:20:58,896
If you want to go to Mars,

319
00:21:00,764 --> 00:21:02,372
I’ll take you there.

320
00:21:06,908 --> 00:21:08,715
Yeah, let’s go.

321
00:21:11,448 --> 00:21:12,751
Hurry up and build that spaceship.

322
00:21:14,248 --> 00:21:15,085
I’ll be waiting.

323
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:18,824
Yes, sir.

324
00:21:23,067 --> 00:21:25,068
Let's compete at this.

325
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:28,873
Shoot the basketball into the hoop.

326
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:29,849
Okay.

327
00:21:31,027 --> 00:21:32,089
Did that go in?

328
00:21:33,134 --> 00:21:33,887
No.

329
00:21:34,065 --> 00:21:35,903
Watch your head.

330
00:21:35,903 --> 00:21:36,928
You’re going to hit your head.

331
00:21:37,173 --> 00:21:39,502
This is called a bed of nails.

332
00:21:39,528 --> 00:21:41,392
It has sharp metal spikes sticking up.

333
00:21:41,703 --> 00:21:43,537
But it won’t hurt you.

334
00:21:43,848 --> 00:21:44,720
Because it distributes your weight.

335
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,220
Mm.

336
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:46,116
Ready?

337
00:21:46,116 --> 00:21:46,616
No.

338
00:21:51,554 --> 00:21:52,619
It won’t hurt.

339
00:21:58,848 --> 00:22:00,035
Hey, come on!

340
00:22:02,169 --> 00:22:03,471
Gosh!

341
00:22:06,162 --> 00:22:06,959
Why are you smiling?

342
00:22:07,488 --> 00:22:08,745
I got these two.

343
00:22:09,034 --> 00:22:10,028
It’s okay. You did well.

344
00:22:10,028 --> 00:22:11,828
Keep practicing. Watch me.

345
00:22:11,828 --> 00:22:12,435
Oh!

346
00:22:14,547 --> 00:22:15,571
Can we take a break?

347
00:22:15,571 --> 00:22:16,743
We’ve been lost for over an hour.

348
00:22:19,996 --> 00:22:21,096
Do whatever you want.

349
00:22:21,096 --> 00:22:22,591
What are you taking me to see?

350
00:22:25,393 --> 00:22:26,153
Cheewa.

351
00:22:27,309 --> 00:22:28,998
It’s an illusion.

352
00:22:29,976 --> 00:22:32,302
It’s an optical illusion that tricks your brain.

353
00:22:32,302 --> 00:22:33,295
This is too much.

354
00:22:33,295 --> 00:22:34,464
I don’t think I can take it anymore.

355
00:22:34,968 --> 00:22:36,931
What did you bring me here for?

356
00:22:36,931 --> 00:22:39,207
If you can’t handle it,
try doing what I’m doing.

357
00:22:39,207 --> 00:22:39,771
What?

358
00:22:47,353 --> 00:22:48,488
Does that really help?

359
00:22:48,732 --> 00:22:49,850
Can you smile too?

360
00:22:53,186 --> 00:22:54,344
I can’t, Cheewa.

361
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:55,702
I’m laughing at you.

362
00:22:55,702 --> 00:22:56,289
Oh my god!

363
00:22:56,289 --> 00:22:57,101
What’s all over my face?

364
00:22:57,101 --> 00:22:59,070
Whoa.

365
00:22:59,070 --> 00:23:00,354
So cool.

366
00:23:00,954 --> 00:23:02,462
So cool.

367
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:04,259
Whoa!

368
00:23:05,124 --> 00:23:05,950
Why are you tilting your head?

369
00:23:05,950 --> 00:23:06,702
You’re scaring me!

370
00:23:07,413 --> 00:23:08,509
Come on, P’Niran.

371
00:23:08,843 --> 00:23:09,807
Damn it.

372
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:13,444
P’Niran, come on.

373
00:23:14,890 --> 00:23:16,338
I’m going to scoot forward like a kid.

374
00:23:19,532 --> 00:23:22,168
Alright, I’m totally fine now.
I don’t have a headache anymore.

375
00:23:24,036 --> 00:23:25,690
Aren’t you tired, Cheewa?

376
00:23:26,246 --> 00:23:27,045
No.

377
00:23:28,268 --> 00:23:29,245
What’s that?

378
00:23:29,779 --> 00:23:31,497
It’s called a kaleidoscope.

379
00:23:32,231 --> 00:23:32,999
Ah.

380
00:23:33,733 --> 00:23:35,548
Try standing on the other side.

381
00:23:37,772 --> 00:23:39,050
You’re giving me orders now?

382
00:23:41,406 --> 00:23:42,924
Now, try leaning down.

383
00:23:44,347 --> 00:23:45,853
Go to the triangle.

384
00:23:51,078 --> 00:23:52,757
Put your face in.

385
00:23:57,106 --> 00:23:58,060
What’s next?

386
00:23:59,238 --> 00:24:00,172
Just look.

387
00:24:02,729 --> 00:24:03,739
I like this one.

388
00:24:04,095 --> 00:24:05,087
So many faces.

389
00:24:05,287 --> 00:24:05,932
It’s funny.

390
00:24:06,243 --> 00:24:09,061
From now on,
if you see triangle mirrors like these,

391
00:24:09,061 --> 00:24:11,373
you’ll only think of my face.

392
00:24:11,373 --> 00:24:12,210
Mm.

393
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:17,825
Why are you smiling?

394
00:24:19,804 --> 00:24:20,703
What are you even smiling about?

395
00:24:21,859 --> 00:24:23,199
Can I get up now?

396
00:24:24,177 --> 00:24:25,688
I can’t stay kneeling.

397
00:24:26,266 --> 00:24:27,400
I’m curious.

398
00:24:28,089 --> 00:24:31,951
Is it possible for two stars
to end up close together?

399
00:24:31,951 --> 00:24:33,055
It’s possible.

400
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:35,896
But the chances are really low.

401
00:24:37,541 --> 00:24:41,925
It's like having two swarms of bees
fly past each other in the middle of the ocean

402
00:24:42,103 --> 00:24:44,760
and hoping they'll crash into each other
midair.

403
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:45,975
I shouldn’t have asked.

404
00:24:46,242 --> 00:24:50,330
If you’re confused, try to imagine it

405
00:24:50,330 --> 00:24:52,079
as two stars kissing each other.

406
00:24:53,235 --> 00:24:57,545
Their surfaces will be pulled toward
each other by gravity

407
00:24:57,812 --> 00:25:00,725
until they end up sharing
the same atmosphere.

408
00:25:01,147 --> 00:25:04,833
Their heat can reach
40,000 degrees Celsius.

409
00:25:05,144 --> 00:25:06,194
After that,

410
00:25:06,528 --> 00:25:08,907
the two stars will merge into one.

411
00:25:11,242 --> 00:25:15,132
So that means if we kiss right now,

412
00:25:20,313 --> 00:25:21,865
we’ll merge into one?

413
00:25:24,289 --> 00:25:27,406
Do you want to try it?

414
00:25:29,532 --> 00:25:31,911
You can find out if the theory is true.

415
00:25:35,024 --> 00:25:37,767
Stand still and lean in.

416
00:25:37,767 --> 00:25:38,414
Hmm?

417
00:25:39,815 --> 00:25:40,522
Here.

418
00:25:40,968 --> 00:25:41,879
Okay.

419
00:25:42,413 --> 00:25:43,811
You have to close your eyes too.

420
00:25:43,811 --> 00:25:44,311
Mm.

421
00:25:45,912 --> 00:25:47,077
Go ahead and flash it.

422
00:25:51,369 --> 00:25:52,155
Done.

423
00:25:53,534 --> 00:25:54,507
Wow.

424
00:25:57,019 --> 00:25:58,588
We really did become one.

425
00:26:05,459 --> 00:26:06,251
Let’s go.

426
00:26:13,845 --> 00:26:15,759
After you graduate from high school,
what would you study?

427
00:26:15,848 --> 00:26:16,989
I’m sorry.

428
00:26:16,989 --> 00:26:18,531
I just wanted to protect you.

429
00:26:18,728 --> 00:26:19,474
Protect me?

430
00:26:19,566 --> 00:26:20,974
Can you stop already?

431
00:26:20,974 --> 00:26:21,715
This is none of your business, nerd!

432
00:26:21,715 --> 00:26:23,184
Stay away from him.

433
00:26:35,180 --> 00:26:36,837
Hey, Thara, play properly.

434
00:26:36,837 --> 00:26:37,447
Sorry.

435
00:26:37,447 --> 00:26:39,188
What’s up, athletes?

436
00:26:40,269 --> 00:26:41,898
Aren’t you two going to eat?

437
00:26:42,047 --> 00:26:43,069
Lunch break is almost over.

438
00:26:43,069 --> 00:26:43,607
Yeah.

439
00:26:43,701 --> 00:26:45,739
No, I’d rather work out.

440
00:26:45,739 --> 00:26:47,187
Then how about we keep score?

441
00:26:47,344 --> 00:26:48,403
Come on, let us join.

442
00:26:48,513 --> 00:26:49,212
Go for it.

443
00:26:49,431 --> 00:26:50,460
Hey, Niran.

444
00:26:51,149 --> 00:26:53,268
Did you really have to
stoop as low as your ranking?

445
00:26:53,613 --> 00:26:54,698
All you can do is attack from behind?

446
00:26:55,184 --> 00:26:55,972
What a loser.

447
00:26:56,332 --> 00:26:57,124
What are you talking about?

448
00:26:57,124 --> 00:26:57,711
Look.

449
00:27:00,917 --> 00:27:01,610
So what?

450
00:27:01,955 --> 00:27:04,751
You did this and still have the nerve
to make that smug face?

451
00:27:05,565 --> 00:27:06,549
Why would I do anything to you?

452
00:27:06,831 --> 00:27:08,880
I don’t even want to see your face.

453
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:09,944
Why the hell would I do that?

454
00:27:09,944 --> 00:27:11,251
Why did you throw a rock at me?

455
00:27:11,705 --> 00:27:12,732
You’ve lost it.

456
00:27:13,672 --> 00:27:14,414
You jerk.

457
00:27:14,649 --> 00:27:17,369
You saw I came to school alone
and threw a rock at me.

458
00:27:17,933 --> 00:27:21,176
When I ran after you,
you ran off and disappeared.

459
00:27:21,380 --> 00:27:22,744
Pathetic.

460
00:27:23,511 --> 00:27:24,218
Hey.

461
00:27:24,531 --> 00:27:25,537
That’s enough, Oy.

462
00:27:26,304 --> 00:27:28,001
What the hell is your problem with Niran?

463
00:27:28,236 --> 00:27:30,124
Wasn’t the fight last time enough?

464
00:27:32,066 --> 00:27:33,748
Go tell the teachers

465
00:27:34,437 --> 00:27:35,961
if you think someone bullied you.

466
00:27:36,478 --> 00:27:38,112
I don’t think you should accuse people.

467
00:27:38,367 --> 00:27:40,191
Why would Niran do that to you?

468
00:27:40,457 --> 00:27:42,017
He could take you down by himself.

469
00:27:42,424 --> 00:27:43,437
He wouldn’t have to run.

470
00:27:44,142 --> 00:27:45,533
Well, ask your friend that!

471
00:27:45,737 --> 00:27:47,133
Ask if he’s ever run away from me before.

472
00:27:47,963 --> 00:27:49,423
Last time you helped that nerd,

473
00:27:49,517 --> 00:27:51,467
you ran away like a scared dog, didn’t you?

474
00:27:51,467 --> 00:27:52,181
Huh?

475
00:27:52,385 --> 00:27:53,236
What?

476
00:27:53,236 --> 00:27:54,116
Hey!

477
00:27:54,116 --> 00:27:55,685
Can you stop already?

478
00:27:56,124 --> 00:27:57,369
This is none of your business, nerd!

479
00:27:58,571 --> 00:28:00,311
Didn’t you just mention me?

480
00:28:02,864 --> 00:28:04,624
Stay away from him.

481
00:28:04,812 --> 00:28:06,904
Get lost before I throw you to the ground.

482
00:28:08,298 --> 00:28:09,972
It won’t be as soft as a boxing ring floor.

483
00:28:14,075 --> 00:28:14,683
Teachers!

484
00:28:14,683 --> 00:28:16,562
This loser is pointing at my friend!

485
00:28:23,367 --> 00:28:24,074
Thank you.

486
00:28:25,625 --> 00:28:27,355
What the f*ck is wrong with Oy?

487
00:28:27,355 --> 00:28:28,226
I don’t get it.

488
00:28:28,226 --> 00:28:30,781
Honestly, when would you even
find the time to bully him?

489
00:28:30,969 --> 00:28:32,699
You study with your friends,
train with me,

490
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:33,969
and go home with Cheewa.

491
00:28:34,251 --> 00:28:36,559
You don’t have time
to do something like that.

492
00:28:36,794 --> 00:28:38,089
With a jerk like Oy,

493
00:28:38,449 --> 00:28:39,712
once he believes you did it,

494
00:28:40,213 --> 00:28:41,427
there’s no changing his mind.

495
00:28:41,646 --> 00:28:43,975
I think you need to find an alibi.

496
00:28:47,546 --> 00:28:49,772
I’m usually not alone.

497
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:52,720
But the point is,

498
00:28:53,206 --> 00:28:55,872
why the hell do I have to deal with this shit?

499
00:28:57,329 --> 00:29:00,440
I’ll tell Teacher Suchart that you didn’t do it

500
00:29:01,630 --> 00:29:02,851
and that you didn’t mess with P’Oy’s group.

501
00:29:03,963 --> 00:29:05,663
I’ll protect you.

502
00:29:07,088 --> 00:29:08,175
Mr. Parncheewa,

503
00:29:09,272 --> 00:29:10,339
as your friend

504
00:29:10,339 --> 00:29:13,147
ever since an asteroid
passed through the solar system

505
00:29:13,147 --> 00:29:14,367
and passed by Earth,

506
00:29:14,367 --> 00:29:16,418
today is the coolest I’ve ever seen you,

507
00:29:16,575 --> 00:29:18,497
for daring to stand up and protect someone.

508
00:29:18,497 --> 00:29:19,896
Someone he cares about.

509
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:24,098
I saw Cheewa staring straight at P’Oy
without even blinking.

510
00:29:24,098 --> 00:29:26,393
Cheewa’s heart must be like
the star Regulus,

511
00:29:26,393 --> 00:29:28,052
standing firmly on the side of what’s right

512
00:29:28,303 --> 00:29:29,999
and always staying by the Moon’s side.

513
00:29:32,552 --> 00:29:33,560
What the hell are you talking about?

514
00:29:34,124 --> 00:29:35,329
Who are you guys?

515
00:29:35,329 --> 00:29:36,453
My name is Jomyut.

516
00:29:36,578 --> 00:29:38,517
I’ve been best friends with Cheewa
since that asteroid.

517
00:29:38,611 --> 00:29:39,361
I’m Newton.

518
00:29:39,361 --> 00:29:41,659
I’m best friends with Jomyut,
who’s best friends with Cheewa.

519
00:29:42,004 --> 00:29:42,668
Ugh.

520
00:29:42,668 --> 00:29:43,438
Let’s just say.

521
00:29:43,438 --> 00:29:45,122
you two are Cheewa’s friends.

522
00:29:45,122 --> 00:29:45,723
That’s it.

523
00:29:46,099 --> 00:29:46,791
Yes.

524
00:29:47,605 --> 00:29:49,232
Now that you two brought that up,

525
00:29:49,483 --> 00:29:50,851
I want to talk about it.

526
00:29:51,180 --> 00:29:53,905
Cheewa,
you don’t have to shield me next time.

527
00:29:53,999 --> 00:29:55,593
You can't even fight. Don’t try to act tough.

528
00:29:55,985 --> 00:29:58,083
What if you end up with a bruised face
or fall and break your glasses?

529
00:29:58,083 --> 00:29:59,040
I’m sorry.

530
00:29:59,495 --> 00:30:01,022
I just wanted to protect you.

531
00:30:01,398 --> 00:30:01,899
Protect me?

532
00:30:02,197 --> 00:30:05,747
Did you know that over 70% of Earth
is covered with water?

533
00:30:05,747 --> 00:30:07,562
Let’s find time to teach you judo.

534
00:30:11,352 --> 00:30:12,700
Are they even talking about the same thing?

535
00:30:14,031 --> 00:30:16,221
It’s a language
only the two of them understand.

536
00:30:19,291 --> 00:30:21,629
Ugh, who even are you guys?

537
00:30:27,110 --> 00:30:29,435
Is your life better with your new schedule?

538
00:30:29,968 --> 00:30:30,914
It’s a bit better than before.

539
00:30:32,684 --> 00:30:35,849
Is it a hassle being my training partner?

540
00:30:36,522 --> 00:30:37,963
Everyone else has already gone home.

541
00:30:39,247 --> 00:30:40,862
Nah, it’s fine.

542
00:30:41,316 --> 00:30:42,058
Thara,

543
00:30:42,591 --> 00:30:43,633
can I ask you something?

544
00:30:44,322 --> 00:30:46,030
Do you still want to keep doing judo?

545
00:30:47,925 --> 00:30:50,150
Lately, you seem like
you don’t really care about it anymore.

546
00:30:51,935 --> 00:30:52,687
I don’t know.

547
00:30:54,018 --> 00:30:57,636
Sometimes I know
I’m not as good as you or Most.

548
00:30:58,952 --> 00:31:00,529
We’ve been doing this since we were kids.

549
00:31:00,717 --> 00:31:02,328
I haven’t gotten anywhere.

550
00:31:04,536 --> 00:31:10,236
If you quit judo, what would you study
after you graduate from high school?

551
00:31:12,397 --> 00:31:14,815
Accounting or business, I guess.

552
00:31:15,457 --> 00:31:17,131
I’ll just do what my family wants
and get it over with.

553
00:31:26,963 --> 00:31:29,259
Alright, stop being emotional.

554
00:31:29,259 --> 00:31:31,323
P’Niran’s guardian is here waiting.

555
00:31:40,975 --> 00:31:44,257
Did you know that our body language
can show how much pain we’re in?

556
00:31:48,689 --> 00:31:50,177
Are you seriously good at everything?

557
00:31:50,522 --> 00:31:52,893
I just want you to stop hurting soon.

558
00:32:00,999 --> 00:32:01,873
I’m just tired.

559
00:32:03,987 --> 00:32:05,196
About what?

560
00:32:09,221 --> 00:32:12,997
Well, I’m tired of what I’m doing right now.

561
00:32:14,814 --> 00:32:16,679
I don’t know if I made the wrong decision.

562
00:32:18,464 --> 00:32:19,886
I’ve been doing judo since I was a kid,

563
00:32:21,233 --> 00:32:22,741
but I’m only starting to have doubts now.

564
00:32:26,014 --> 00:32:27,935
I’m unlucky this year, too.

565
00:32:30,645 --> 00:32:32,002
I couldn’t get into the Athletes’ Village.

566
00:32:35,343 --> 00:32:38,109
Did you know my family has let me try
so many things since I was a kid?

567
00:32:39,973 --> 00:32:43,016
Sports like basketball and football.

568
00:32:43,157 --> 00:32:43,968
Drums.

569
00:32:44,767 --> 00:32:45,647
Piano lessons.

570
00:32:47,198 --> 00:32:48,209
And so much more.

571
00:32:52,610 --> 00:32:54,141
You know what you sound like?

572
00:32:54,783 --> 00:32:56,293
Like that ad that talks about

573
00:32:56,293 --> 00:32:59,238
planting trees, diving, seeing coral reefs,
and stuff like that.

574
00:33:00,460 --> 00:33:02,306
I don’t talk like that ad.

575
00:33:02,682 --> 00:33:03,651
I’ve actually done all those things.

576
00:33:07,394 --> 00:33:09,326
I just feel lucky that

577
00:33:10,673 --> 00:33:12,862
my family lets me try so many things.

578
00:33:14,365 --> 00:33:15,077
Mm.

579
00:33:16,863 --> 00:33:17,903
You’re lucky. Good for you.

580
00:33:25,382 --> 00:33:27,693
I want to be your good luck.

581
00:33:40,979 --> 00:33:42,675
We might not get to see the simulated stars,

582
00:33:44,930 --> 00:33:46,725
but we ended up seeing the real ones.

583
00:33:49,701 --> 00:33:50,879
This is so freaking good.

584
00:34:08,084 --> 00:34:08,939
Do you want to wait inside?

585
00:34:09,111 --> 00:34:09,874
There are a lot of mosquitoes out here.

586
00:34:10,234 --> 00:34:12,174
You promised me earlier.

587
00:34:12,174 --> 00:34:12,969
What promise?

588
00:34:13,367 --> 00:34:14,390
Cheewa,

589
00:34:14,703 --> 00:34:16,030
I want to ask you something.

590
00:34:16,312 --> 00:34:17,670
How do you feel about my friend?

591
00:34:28,457 --> 00:34:29,366
Honestly,

592
00:34:29,366 --> 00:34:30,643
it’s nice being a 12th-grader.

593
00:34:30,643 --> 00:34:31,681
We have so many fewer classes.

594
00:34:31,681 --> 00:34:33,429
We have fewer classes,
but we have so much more to read.

595
00:34:33,635 --> 00:34:34,662
Is that really a good thing?

596
00:34:35,653 --> 00:34:36,552
Hey, Niran.

597
00:34:36,679 --> 00:34:39,992
Why is Parncheewa being so clingy with you?

598
00:34:39,992 --> 00:34:41,126
Just say you’re flirting with each other.

599
00:34:41,537 --> 00:34:42,474
Shut up, Hem.

600
00:34:42,999 --> 00:34:44,117
Flirting, my ass.

601
00:34:44,323 --> 00:34:45,553
Don’t say that to Cheewa.

602
00:34:45,759 --> 00:34:46,869
You’ll make him feel awkward.

603
00:34:47,262 --> 00:34:48,804
I won’t feel awkward.

604
00:34:49,813 --> 00:34:52,257
People naturally have a gravitational pull
toward each other.

605
00:34:52,257 --> 00:34:55,490
Just like each planet
orbiting around the Sun.

606
00:34:55,490 --> 00:34:57,271
Without these forces,

607
00:34:57,271 --> 00:34:59,436
Earth might drift out of its orbit.

608
00:35:00,595 --> 00:35:03,021
There’s one more interesting theory.

609
00:35:03,021 --> 00:35:05,626
Like how planets are formed—

610
00:35:05,626 --> 00:35:06,580
Hold on.

611
00:35:07,159 --> 00:35:08,223
One question.

612
00:35:09,120 --> 00:35:10,788
What are you doing here?

613
00:35:12,302 --> 00:35:13,568
We’re here to study.

614
00:35:16,129 --> 00:35:18,352
You're the only one with your mouth
wide open and those doe eyes.

615
00:35:21,212 --> 00:35:21,725
Huh?

616
00:35:22,304 --> 00:35:23,012
Me?

617
00:35:23,218 --> 00:35:24,057
I’m doe-eyed?

618
00:35:24,337 --> 00:35:25,007
Yeah.

619
00:35:25,680 --> 00:35:27,853
If you don’t believe us, ask Jomyut.

620
00:35:27,853 --> 00:35:30,034
You look so focused
on what Cheewa’s saying.

621
00:35:30,595 --> 00:35:31,344
That’s right.

622
00:35:31,979 --> 00:35:33,603
You seem to be interested in my friend.

623
00:35:33,603 --> 00:35:36,630
I mean, really interested in
what my friend’s saying.

624
00:35:36,630 --> 00:35:40,213
He’s just been telling me this and that
since we went to the planetarium.

625
00:35:40,213 --> 00:35:41,197
The planetarium?

626
00:35:42,823 --> 00:35:44,626
You went to the planetarium with him?

627
00:35:44,888 --> 00:35:45,651
How?

628
00:35:45,763 --> 00:35:46,431
When?

629
00:35:46,992 --> 00:35:48,106
Tell us your schedule.

630
00:35:48,106 --> 00:35:50,333
Oh, it’s not the planetarium.

631
00:35:51,118 --> 00:35:53,187
It was some kind of science event, right?

632
00:35:53,187 --> 00:35:54,602
Something like that.

633
00:35:54,602 --> 00:35:55,230
What was it?

634
00:35:57,473 --> 00:35:58,968
But we just went there.

635
00:35:59,267 --> 00:36:01,185
There’s nothing unusual about it.

636
00:36:01,970 --> 00:36:04,630
Well, you didn’t tell us at all.

637
00:36:05,284 --> 00:36:07,362
Do I have to tell you guys everything?

638
00:36:07,362 --> 00:36:08,209
No.

639
00:36:08,209 --> 00:36:12,432
I mean, we don’t usually meet up
on weekends anyway.

640
00:36:12,675 --> 00:36:14,249
We’re not middle schoolers anymore.

641
00:36:14,810 --> 00:36:16,426
We’re grownups
and we’re going to university soon.

642
00:36:16,931 --> 00:36:17,627
Yeah.

643
00:36:22,599 --> 00:36:24,849
By the way, Cheewa.

644
00:36:25,447 --> 00:36:26,414
There’s something

645
00:36:26,863 --> 00:36:28,502
I want to ask you.

646
00:36:29,175 --> 00:36:30,789
How do you feel about my friend?

647
00:36:32,999 --> 00:36:34,084
If you don’t answer,

648
00:36:34,420 --> 00:36:36,120
I won’t let you sit with us anymore.

649
00:36:36,270 --> 00:36:36,882
Hey.

650
00:36:37,517 --> 00:36:38,798
Can you not be so extra?

651
00:36:39,602 --> 00:36:42,038
Whatever creative feelings Parncheewa
has for P’Niran,

652
00:36:42,393 --> 00:36:43,963
that’s up to him.

653
00:36:44,206 --> 00:36:45,227
What? You kid.

654
00:36:45,489 --> 00:36:46,630
Stop it, guys.

655
00:36:46,855 --> 00:36:48,771
Don’t make him feel any more uncomfortable
than he already is.

656
00:36:49,986 --> 00:36:51,067
Don't overthink it.

657
00:36:51,067 --> 00:36:53,249
Sit with whoever you want.

658
00:36:53,660 --> 00:36:54,572
And Hem,

659
00:36:56,179 --> 00:36:59,272
you pressed him about it because
you’re upset I didn’t invite you, aren’t you?

660
00:36:59,272 --> 00:37:00,727
I’ll invite you next time.

661
00:37:00,727 --> 00:37:03,150
This time, I was just stressed out, so I…

662
00:37:03,430 --> 00:37:04,880
spontaneously went there to relax.

663
00:37:05,572 --> 00:37:08,064
Oh, I’m not upset.

664
00:37:08,214 --> 00:37:09,657
Yeah, stop it.

665
00:37:09,657 --> 00:37:10,316
Quiet.

666
00:37:11,101 --> 00:37:12,243
Or I’ll throw you.

667
00:37:19,046 --> 00:37:19,823
Let’s go.

668
00:37:20,478 --> 00:37:23,243
Jomyut, go to the restroom.

669
00:37:23,430 --> 00:37:24,775
I don’t need to go.

670
00:37:24,868 --> 00:37:26,081
Just go.

671
00:37:27,072 --> 00:37:28,505
Fine, I need to go.

672
00:37:34,280 --> 00:37:35,045
Cheewa,

673
00:37:35,475 --> 00:37:37,073
ignore what Hem said.

674
00:37:37,073 --> 00:37:38,628
He just rambles. He talks a lot.

675
00:37:38,759 --> 00:37:39,710
What about you?

676
00:37:41,168 --> 00:37:42,347
Are you uncomfortable with me?

677
00:37:43,375 --> 00:37:44,023
No.

678
00:37:44,154 --> 00:37:47,416
How do you feel about what my friend said?

679
00:37:47,809 --> 00:37:48,637
What do you mean?

680
00:37:48,899 --> 00:37:50,750
The fact that I’m hitting on you.

681
00:37:57,609 --> 00:37:58,753
You’re down bad, Glasses.

682
00:38:01,258 --> 00:38:03,462
You promised me earlier.

683
00:38:04,116 --> 00:38:04,894
What promise?

684
00:38:05,212 --> 00:38:07,159
You said you’d teach me judo.

685
00:38:08,150 --> 00:38:08,887
Oh.

686
00:38:10,513 --> 00:38:13,071
Well, just let me know when.

687
00:38:16,529 --> 00:38:18,857
Are you still scared the guys
from the Boxing Club will bully you?

688
00:38:19,585 --> 00:38:22,761
Even if I’m not scared,
I still want to walk home with you every day.

689
00:38:24,032 --> 00:38:25,457
Once you learn judo,

690
00:38:25,924 --> 00:38:27,790
you won’t have to be scared anymore.

691
00:38:27,790 --> 00:38:30,709
If they start messing with you,
just hit them and throw them down.

692
00:38:34,167 --> 00:38:35,911
Oh, I want to return the shirt
I borrowed from you.

693
00:38:35,911 --> 00:38:36,798
I’ll go grab it.

694
00:38:38,293 --> 00:38:40,479
Or do you want to wait inside?

695
00:38:40,853 --> 00:38:42,027
There are a lot of mosquitoes out here.

696
00:38:42,999 --> 00:38:45,554
Oh, I have mosquito spray.

697
00:38:46,264 --> 00:38:47,249
Just come in.

698
00:39:20,342 --> 00:39:21,100
You like that?

699
00:39:23,960 --> 00:39:24,734
No.

700
00:39:27,854 --> 00:39:28,526
Here.

701
00:39:29,498 --> 00:39:30,380
You can smell it.

702
00:39:30,511 --> 00:39:31,445
I guarantee it doesn’t smell bad.

703
00:39:34,865 --> 00:39:37,857
Sunlight reacts with the detergent,

704
00:39:38,679 --> 00:39:41,124
creating a subtle, pleasant scent
known as the sun-dried smell.

705
00:39:47,946 --> 00:39:49,095
I have a secret to tell.

706
00:39:52,176 --> 00:39:53,128
I hung this out at night.

707
00:40:00,836 --> 00:40:01,561
Just kidding.

708
00:40:01,879 --> 00:40:02,977
Oh, your face fell.

709
00:40:08,136 --> 00:40:08,903
Isn’t that cute?

710
00:40:09,651 --> 00:40:10,768
I drew it when I was a kid.

711
00:40:11,273 --> 00:40:12,489
It’s heartwarming.

712
00:40:13,704 --> 00:40:16,589
But why is there a guitar too?

713
00:40:20,514 --> 00:40:23,346
My dad told me that back in the day,

714
00:40:25,533 --> 00:40:26,836
he played guitar to win my mom over.

715
00:40:32,217 --> 00:40:33,053
Uh…

716
00:40:33,931 --> 00:40:35,825
What are you going to do next?

717
00:40:37,002 --> 00:40:38,036
Probably nothing.

718
00:40:38,354 --> 00:40:39,323
I think I’ll just lie around.

719
00:40:39,921 --> 00:40:41,487
You should go home.

720
00:40:41,487 --> 00:40:42,223
Here’s your shirt.

721
00:40:44,298 --> 00:40:45,086
Okay.

722
00:40:46,245 --> 00:40:48,689
Thank you for letting me borrow it.

723
00:40:49,979 --> 00:40:50,813
You’re welcome.

724
00:40:52,495 --> 00:40:53,239
I’ll walk you out.

725
00:40:57,332 --> 00:40:58,752
You’re not going to bed yet, right?

726
00:41:00,303 --> 00:41:00,994
Why?

727
00:41:01,181 --> 00:41:01,951
What’s up?

728
00:41:01,951 --> 00:41:02,860
You don’t want to leave yet?

729
00:41:14,851 --> 00:41:15,893
He actually came?

730
00:41:24,752 --> 00:41:25,379
What’s that?

731
00:41:26,463 --> 00:41:28,745
A spacescope or a kaleidoscope.

732
00:41:28,951 --> 00:41:29,729
I don’t know.

733
00:41:29,729 --> 00:41:31,913
Just tell me.
I don’t know the exact name.

734
00:41:32,249 --> 00:41:34,050
That wasn’t a question.

735
00:41:34,405 --> 00:41:36,489
I mean, it has two names.

736
00:42:02,509 --> 00:42:05,016
(You’ll see the person you like in there.)

737
00:42:07,652 --> 00:42:10,475
(From now on, if you see triangle mirrors
like these,)

738
00:42:11,484 --> 00:42:13,255
(you’ll only think of my face.)

739
00:42:16,619 --> 00:42:17,607
(I like this one.)

740
00:42:17,999 --> 00:42:19,192
(So many faces.)

741
00:42:21,716 --> 00:42:23,790
Can I ask for something before I leave?

742
00:42:24,425 --> 00:42:27,509
Just say what you want and hurry home.

743
00:42:27,509 --> 00:42:28,413
There are a lot of mosquitoes out here.

744
00:42:31,404 --> 00:42:33,029
Can I get a good night kiss?

745
00:42:33,029 --> 00:42:33,786
Huh?

746
00:43:22,615 --> 00:43:24,860
Now, touch your cheek.

747
00:43:30,935 --> 00:43:32,303
That’s my kiss.

748
00:43:40,502 --> 00:43:42,517
And this is yours.

749
00:43:49,502 --> 00:43:54,186
(Well, if we kiss right now,)

750
00:43:57,382 --> 00:43:59,666
(we’ll merge into one.)

751
00:44:07,281 --> 00:44:09,831
The thing is
I see Cheewa in my mind all the time.

752
00:44:09,831 --> 00:44:10,908
I’m already hitting on you.

753
00:44:10,908 --> 00:44:12,462
I’m hitting on you!

754
00:44:12,462 --> 00:44:14,888
The Astronomy Club has an activity today?

755
00:44:14,888 --> 00:44:16,916
I’m exploring with the other club members.

756
00:44:16,916 --> 00:44:18,091
Do you guys want to go up?

757
00:44:18,091 --> 00:44:18,703
Let’s go.

758
00:44:18,703 --> 00:44:19,755
We’re all here anyway.

759
00:44:19,755 --> 00:44:22,019
Is that the face of someone excited to see aliens?

760
00:44:22,019 --> 00:44:23,964
I’m not talking about aliens.

761
00:44:23,964 --> 00:44:26,640
I’m talking about being with you.
